Article 26 (Detailed terms and conditions of transactions of information security products and information security services)
Where an information security enterprise intends to prepare the terms and conditions for protecting users pursuant to Article 36 (2) of the Act, it shall include details regarding the following:
Methods and procedures for returning amounts erroneously paid or overpaid;
Methods of cancelling or terminating a contract for using an information security product and information security service;
Compensation to users for loss which incurred due to a defect, etc in the product;
Methods and procedures for resolving disputes;
Other matters the information security enterprise deems necessary to protect users.

